==== simple
h3: Configuration Files
config._group_dhcp [CBI.FlagValue] DHCP and DNS: [ ]
  help: /etc/config/dhcp: address pools, static leases, DNS settings.
config._group_firewall [CBI.FlagValue] Firewall: [x]
  help: /etc/config/firewall: zones, rules, port forwards. Review the rules before enabling: they apply to every node.
config._group_others [CBI.DummyValue] Other files: text "3 groups (2 enabled) Advanced Config Sync →"
h3: DHCP Leases
config.lease_sync [CBI.FlagValue] Real-time Lease Sync: [x]
  help: Replicates DHCP leases between nodes so that clients keep their address after a failover. Independent of the DHCP configuration sync above.
config._dhcp_authoritative [CBI.DummyValue] : text "dnsmasq is authoritativeSeveral nodes serve DHCP, so an authoritative dnsmasq rejects the clients of the other nodes. Turn off Authoritative in DHCP and DNS on every node.Go to DHCP and DNS…"
